<title>UK: EBRD sets 6.0 bln Taiwan dollar seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>EBRD sets 6.0 bln Taiwan dollar seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development has issued a 6.0 billion Taiwan dollar ($215 million) seven-year bond into the domestic market, it said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Taipei-listed notes carry a 6.04 percent coupon and were priced to yield 26 basis points over government bonds. Fees were 0.25 point.</p>
<p>Grand Cathay Securities Corp (books) and Chinatrust Commercial Bank were joint lead managers, the EBRD said.</p>
<p>The EBRD said the proceeds were swapped into U.S.dollars at &quot;competitive rates&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
